WEBVTT

01:20.207 --> 01:22.497
-Enjoy.
-If it's this season…

01:23.757 --> 01:25.127
That goes outside.

01:25.217 --> 01:26.257
Got it.

01:28.047 --> 01:29.427
Thank you.

01:31.047 --> 01:31.887
Morning.

01:31.967 --> 01:34.677
It's also good for storing genomes.

01:38.517 --> 01:40.017
SPANISH GRAMMAR

01:51.237 --> 01:53.657
MOVING CENTER

01:54.247 --> 01:56.117
Thanks for your help.

02:36.947 --> 02:40.367
How was the dive yesterday, Tsuneo?

02:41.287 --> 02:43.167
I saw a Priolepis nocturna.

02:43.247 --> 02:45.247
That's awesome!

02:45.337 --> 02:48.337
I was lucky the sea was so calm.

02:49.757 --> 02:52.637
You're on summer break from college?

02:53.217 --> 02:54.047
That's right.

02:54.637 --> 02:57.967
How about doing a dive next Wednesday?

02:58.057 --> 02:58.887
Sure!

02:59.977 --> 03:01.897
Bring some girls too.

03:01.977 --> 03:03.057
Sorry?

03:03.647 --> 03:07.027
At this rate, fish will be our only love.

03:07.107 --> 03:09.897
But I long for a human one. Right, Tsuneo?

03:10.487 --> 03:11.817
No time for that.

03:12.527 --> 03:15.157
I start another part-time job next week.

03:16.407 --> 03:19.157
You're wasting your youth.

03:19.247 --> 03:21.957
The summer of 22 comes only once.

03:22.537 --> 03:23.787
Whatever.

03:23.877 --> 03:25.337
Tsuneo!

03:26.997 --> 03:28.507
Thank you.

03:31.757 --> 03:35.507
UNDER CONSTRUCTION

03:39.177 --> 03:40.927
Is this the right way?

03:41.597 --> 03:43.847
Help!

04:07.997 --> 04:09.297
That hurts.

04:11.877 --> 04:14.177
Are you okay?

04:22.307 --> 04:23.767
Kumiko!

04:24.347 --> 04:27.017
Kumiko, are you all right?

04:33.487 --> 04:36.777
Did you save her, young man? Thank you.

04:36.867 --> 04:37.697
No.

04:38.697 --> 04:40.447
Are you injured?

04:40.537 --> 04:42.117
I think I'm fine.

04:42.787 --> 04:46.667
I turn away for one second,
and someone pushes her.

04:47.377 --> 04:49.707
I almost had a heart attack.

04:50.457 --> 04:53.047
That hurts! Why did you do that?

04:53.127 --> 04:54.167
Pervert.

04:54.257 --> 04:55.087
What?

04:55.177 --> 04:58.257
Stop groping me, you pervert!

05:05.387 --> 05:07.937
The pervert is following us, Grandma.

05:09.477 --> 05:10.937
My house is this way.

05:13.857 --> 05:14.897
Shall I push?

05:14.987 --> 05:15.817
No.

05:20.987 --> 05:22.197
Born this way.

05:25.707 --> 05:27.827
What about our walk, Grandma?

05:27.917 --> 05:31.957
We're giving up walks for a while.

05:32.047 --> 05:33.167
I don't want to.

05:33.247 --> 05:37.257
Tough. You can't have everything your way.

05:40.467 --> 05:43.177
Do you always take walks at this hour?

05:44.217 --> 05:48.767
I thought it'd be safer
and we wouldn't be seen.

05:49.647 --> 05:52.977
But the world is full of scary beasts.

05:54.857 --> 05:55.737
Here we are.

06:07.617 --> 06:09.207
I'll be going.

06:09.707 --> 06:10.747
Come on in.

06:12.037 --> 06:14.247
You haven't eaten yet, have you?

06:20.047 --> 06:20.927
Oh, drat.

06:21.507 --> 06:23.887
Would octopus dumplings do?

06:23.967 --> 06:25.847
We're out of rice.

06:26.517 --> 06:27.347
That's fine.

06:38.357 --> 06:39.737
Not you again.

06:40.407 --> 06:42.407
I keep putting him out but he returns.

06:43.027 --> 06:46.537
Don't touch it, Kumiko. It may have fleas.

06:46.617 --> 06:47.447
Scat!

06:49.077 --> 06:51.167
Just here for some free food.

06:51.707 --> 06:53.917
Do you feed him often?

06:54.497 --> 06:55.457
I meant you.

06:58.757 --> 07:01.837
No, he's not a friend. Just a pervert.

07:02.837 --> 07:04.297
He understands you.

07:04.387 --> 07:06.767
Of course not. Are you stupid?

07:09.807 --> 07:12.307
"You're intruding on my territory."

07:12.397 --> 07:13.477
That's what he said.

07:15.227 --> 07:16.107
Ms. Kumiko…

07:16.187 --> 07:17.357
Josee.

07:17.437 --> 07:18.527
What?

07:19.107 --> 07:21.397
I'm not Kumiko. I'm Josee.

07:21.987 --> 07:22.817
Josee?

07:32.667 --> 07:33.497
With thanks.

07:40.917 --> 07:42.257
Have seconds.

07:43.257 --> 07:48.427
Thank you. I can't afford
to buy another box lunch.

07:48.517 --> 07:51.477
You sound very poor. Are you a student?

07:52.097 --> 07:54.977
Yes, I rent an apartment nearby.

07:55.557 --> 08:00.187
I'm poor, but I'm also trying
to save money.

08:00.277 --> 08:01.817
Nobody's asking.

08:03.067 --> 08:05.117
I'm thirsty, Grandma.

08:05.197 --> 08:07.117
Barley tea or water?

08:07.197 --> 08:08.867
-Barley tea.
-Okay.

08:08.947 --> 08:11.037
Just a second.

08:11.117 --> 08:12.657
Allow me.

08:12.747 --> 08:16.587
It's okay. Don't let your food get cold.

08:17.167 --> 08:18.167
Is this it?

08:21.257 --> 08:22.257
Here.

08:23.507 --> 08:24.887
You're pretty demanding.

08:25.547 --> 08:27.427
Ouch, that's hot!

08:31.347 --> 08:32.557
What's the deal?

08:33.557 --> 08:37.017
Kumiko can't hold onto tea in a cup.

08:37.977 --> 08:41.777
How about a plastic bottle? Or a thermos.

08:42.987 --> 08:44.397
You're a funny young man.

08:46.447 --> 08:47.987
Thank you for the meal.

08:48.617 --> 08:50.157
Sorry for staying so long.

08:50.237 --> 08:53.447
Nonsense. We don't often have guests.

08:53.537 --> 08:54.367
Goodbye.

08:57.417 --> 09:00.127
Do you want to earn some money?

09:02.007 --> 09:03.297
A new job?

09:03.877 --> 09:06.837
Yeah, someone I happened to meet.

09:06.927 --> 09:08.507
It pays really well.

09:09.177 --> 09:10.887
What about this job?

09:11.467 --> 09:12.807
I'll continue, of course.

09:14.597 --> 09:17.687
Where's the joy in working so much?

09:17.767 --> 09:21.567
I can introduce you too. She's a female.

09:21.647 --> 09:23.107
-Seriously?
-Yes.

09:23.187 --> 09:24.987
About 80 years old.

09:25.067 --> 09:26.237
Figures.

09:26.817 --> 09:29.067
Move those hands, Hayato.

09:29.157 --> 09:30.237
Yes, boss.

09:32.117 --> 09:33.997
Have you seen the toolbox?

09:34.577 --> 09:38.537
Yeah, the lid needed fixing.

09:38.627 --> 09:39.497
Hey, thanks!

09:41.877 --> 09:46.127
I might even hire you full-time
when you graduate.

09:46.217 --> 09:47.927
I'll think about it.

09:48.007 --> 09:50.847
Not you. I meant Tsuneo Suzukawa here.

09:51.427 --> 09:54.807
I plan to study abroad after college.

09:55.887 --> 10:00.607
Didn't you know, boss?
He's going to the Netherlands.

10:00.687 --> 10:01.937
It's Mexico.

10:02.017 --> 10:06.817
Ah, Mexico. I once swam
with a baby sea lion in La Paz.

10:07.607 --> 10:11.567
Study abroad, huh?
We're going to miss you.

10:12.157 --> 10:14.907
I haven't found a school yet.

10:14.997 --> 10:20.077
And he hasn't saved enough.
You should raise his wages.

10:20.167 --> 10:21.707
Mine too, while you're at it.

10:21.787 --> 10:23.587
Go check the machines.

10:23.667 --> 10:25.047
Right away, sir!

10:26.667 --> 10:28.127
What's wrong, Mai?

10:28.217 --> 10:33.427
Nothing. Well, tell me
about that job that pays so well.

10:33.507 --> 10:36.057
You are to do as Kumiko says.

10:37.017 --> 10:37.847
What?

10:37.927 --> 10:39.727
Didn't I tell you?

10:39.807 --> 10:44.147
No, you didn't.
You mean I'd be working here?

10:44.817 --> 10:46.857
Yes, you'd be working here.

10:49.607 --> 10:52.117
Don't look so disappointed.

10:52.197 --> 10:56.747
There's only one rule.
Don't take her out on your own.

10:57.497 --> 10:59.867
Help yourself to anything in the fridge.

11:00.537 --> 11:01.997
There's plenty.

11:02.667 --> 11:06.167
I have to go.
Kumiko will tell you what to do.

11:06.797 --> 11:08.297
Where are you going?

11:19.427 --> 11:20.267
Well… hello.

11:22.057 --> 11:23.057
What do I do?

11:25.687 --> 11:26.567
Joan, was it?

11:26.647 --> 11:27.527
It's Josee!

11:32.487 --> 11:33.907
-Josee?
-Stay away.

11:38.697 --> 11:41.457
"Intruders get out", he says.

11:42.327 --> 11:45.337
But I'm working here from today.

11:47.087 --> 11:48.167
-Kneel.
-What?

11:48.667 --> 11:49.707
On your knees.

11:51.417 --> 11:52.257
Okay, I'm kneeling.

11:57.467 --> 11:58.847
Do you want to live?

12:00.807 --> 12:03.097
Why am I kneeling?

12:03.187 --> 12:06.267
To see how long a human can endure it.

12:07.397 --> 12:09.027
Do your job well.

12:13.817 --> 12:16.317
I'm going to make her cry.

12:16.407 --> 12:20.247
Your look has really changed
in the past month.

12:20.827 --> 12:23.577
Is working for this Josee that hard?

12:23.657 --> 12:25.747
It's way beyond hard.

12:26.417 --> 12:27.837
Count the meshes in the tatami mats.

12:29.207 --> 12:32.337
It keeps me up at night wondering.

12:33.467 --> 12:36.847
5,208, 5,209, 5,210,

12:37.427 --> 12:40.427
5,211, 5,212…

12:40.517 --> 12:42.847
Oh, what a waste.

12:43.477 --> 12:47.187
I squandered 8,000 yen
on a bad pachinko machine.

12:47.267 --> 12:50.687
8,001, 8,002, 8,003… Oops.

12:50.777 --> 12:52.237
Start over.

12:55.317 --> 12:57.657
Bring me four-leaf clovers.

12:59.117 --> 13:01.657
Four-leaf clovers.

13:02.247 --> 13:04.917
Four-leaf clovers…

13:05.867 --> 13:07.207
Here.

13:08.537 --> 13:09.747
Nothing's happening.

13:11.417 --> 13:14.007
Ten are supposed to grant my wish.

13:14.087 --> 13:15.127
Superstition.

13:15.797 --> 13:17.047
What wish?

13:17.137 --> 13:19.467
Don't speak to me. I'm busy.

13:23.177 --> 13:25.597
She looks so meek

13:25.687 --> 13:29.607
until she speaks
and becomes a stinging jellyfish.

13:30.187 --> 13:33.727
I'd like to glue her
to one of her sliding doors.

13:33.817 --> 13:35.277
Oh, harsh.

13:35.357 --> 13:40.157
Why don't you quit?
You need to write your thesis.

13:40.987 --> 13:43.537
But I really need the money.

13:43.617 --> 13:46.327
You don't have to earn it there.

13:46.917 --> 13:49.787
Even if your hours
at the shop are decreasing.

13:50.877 --> 13:53.167
Stop thinking about making a buck

13:53.247 --> 13:56.337
and give some attention to Mai.

13:57.047 --> 13:58.587
Eat this and shut up.

14:02.387 --> 14:03.927
Is Tsuneo here?

14:04.637 --> 14:05.477
Professor!

14:06.137 --> 14:09.017
There you are. Can you spare a second?

14:11.057 --> 14:13.607
Your essay on Turing Patterns.

14:14.317 --> 14:18.527
I sent it to a professor
at Mexico City University.

14:18.607 --> 14:22.527
He loved it and wants you to study there.

14:22.617 --> 14:23.827
Thank you!

14:24.617 --> 14:27.867
That leaves the question of a scholarship.

14:27.957 --> 14:31.457
It'll be hard to pay your own way.

14:32.037 --> 14:33.747
I'll study Spanish harder,

14:33.837 --> 14:38.297
and rewrite my research proposal.

14:38.377 --> 14:40.887
Okay, don't push yourself too hard.

14:40.967 --> 14:43.137
You'll need your health.

14:43.847 --> 14:45.597
Otherwise, all will be lost.

14:46.977 --> 14:47.807
Okay.

16:24.237 --> 16:26.027
I thought you were asleep.

16:27.947 --> 16:31.577
Grandma, can we resume our walks?

16:31.657 --> 16:32.537
No.

16:33.117 --> 16:35.377
What if you get pushed again?

16:35.957 --> 16:39.297
Can you protect yourself?

16:40.547 --> 16:42.127
Listen to me. The world…

16:42.717 --> 16:44.877
-is full of scary beasts.
-Is full of scary beasts.

16:45.387 --> 16:46.967
Yes, I know that.

16:48.347 --> 16:50.767
Then be content to stay home.

16:58.147 --> 17:01.897
I envy you. Free to go where you choose.

17:06.567 --> 17:08.487
Nothing will happen from waiting.

17:23.417 --> 17:24.297
Hello!

17:39.227 --> 17:42.937
I'll miss the money, but Hayato is right.

17:50.027 --> 17:52.447
Listen, I've come to a decision.

17:55.037 --> 17:57.077
I need to quit this job.

18:00.537 --> 18:01.377
Are you listening?

18:36.787 --> 18:38.247
Kumiko!

18:40.247 --> 18:41.877
Kumiko!

18:44.127 --> 18:45.507
What's wrong?

18:45.587 --> 18:47.627
Kumiko is missing!

19:02.897 --> 19:03.727
Stop!

19:05.017 --> 19:06.527
What are you doing?

19:07.147 --> 19:08.857
None of your business!

19:11.407 --> 19:12.947
Let me go!

19:16.787 --> 19:17.827
What, by yourself?

19:29.217 --> 19:30.967
-Let's call it a day.
-Take me.

19:33.007 --> 19:34.637
Take me to the sea.

19:35.507 --> 19:38.847
Or I'll say you
groped my breasts and get you fired.

19:41.187 --> 19:43.977
Do what you want. I'm going home.

19:59.617 --> 20:01.157
This will cost extra.

20:09.047 --> 20:10.467
280 yen.

20:11.417 --> 20:13.967
For the ticket. I've got a railcard.

20:15.387 --> 20:16.217
Is something wrong?

20:16.297 --> 20:17.847
No, it's nothing.

20:19.767 --> 20:23.637
It's Tsuneo. I've found Kumiko.

20:25.397 --> 20:26.227
Excuse me.

20:35.277 --> 20:39.907
I'll have her back
as soon as I can. Please understand.

20:44.537 --> 20:45.667
-Tiger.
-What?

20:46.377 --> 20:47.627
Tigers everywhere.

20:47.707 --> 20:48.917
Tigers?

20:52.627 --> 20:53.587
Hey.

20:53.667 --> 20:54.717
Where to now?

20:54.797 --> 20:55.637
Home.

20:56.427 --> 20:58.137
What about the sea?

20:58.717 --> 21:00.257
You were so insistent.

21:01.807 --> 21:03.267
Watch where you're going!

21:03.847 --> 21:05.977
What? She bumped into me.

21:09.147 --> 21:12.187
Are you serious? What a jerk.

21:13.317 --> 21:14.737
Hey, watch it!!

21:14.817 --> 21:15.657
Yes, Granny.

21:15.737 --> 21:18.817
Mess with me and I'll rip out your heart

21:18.907 --> 21:19.987
and feed it to you!

21:20.987 --> 21:21.827
Sorry!

21:30.667 --> 21:33.007
What do you want to do, Ms. Josee?

21:33.837 --> 21:35.507
Are we going or not?

21:46.347 --> 21:47.187
Be careful.

21:52.267 --> 21:53.277
Not there?

21:53.357 --> 21:54.687
No, it's this way.

21:54.777 --> 21:55.947
Really?

21:58.027 --> 21:59.617
Now, where's the elevator?

22:00.237 --> 22:02.197
Why are there so many people?

22:02.277 --> 22:03.617
Beats me.

22:12.417 --> 22:15.257
It's not my first time on a train.

22:17.167 --> 22:18.717
Stop staring.

22:18.797 --> 22:23.307
No, I was just wondering
how you see the world.

22:25.017 --> 22:28.017
Forests, deserts, New York, Paris…

22:28.687 --> 22:30.897
I've never imagined them that way.

22:32.057 --> 22:33.817
The way you drew them.

22:33.897 --> 22:36.027
You went into my room?

22:36.607 --> 22:39.527
I'd like to see an ocean like that.

22:45.367 --> 22:47.407
Pretty cocky for a servant.

22:48.287 --> 22:49.327
A servant?

22:49.417 --> 22:52.417
From today, you're "My Servant."

22:52.497 --> 22:53.587
What is that?

22:54.547 --> 22:55.627
Look! An airplane!

22:55.707 --> 22:59.297
Really? Where? Point it out to me.

23:41.757 --> 23:42.927
It's like a dream.

23:53.097 --> 23:54.937
Give it up. It's sand.

23:57.607 --> 23:58.437
You okay?

23:59.987 --> 24:01.447
Take it easy.

24:04.777 --> 24:05.617
Hey!

24:07.697 --> 24:09.447
I need an answer.

24:11.077 --> 24:16.877
My dad once asked me,
"How does the sea taste?"

24:18.587 --> 24:23.427
When I was a child,
he took me to the ocean.

24:24.257 --> 24:27.597
But the waves were too scary to get near.

24:29.557 --> 24:34.137
My dad died without
ever telling me the answer to it.

24:36.517 --> 24:41.437
Of course, I learned
from books that the sea is salty.

24:43.277 --> 24:46.067
But this may be
my only chance to confirm it.

24:57.127 --> 24:59.247
What are you doing?

24:59.337 --> 25:02.297
Put me down, you pervert!

25:02.917 --> 25:04.627
You want to see for yourself?

25:16.147 --> 25:16.977
Salty.

25:19.647 --> 25:21.227
It really is salty!

25:21.817 --> 25:23.317
Why is it so salty?

25:24.067 --> 25:25.237
I'm happy for you.

25:28.617 --> 25:29.987
Hey, stay still!

25:30.077 --> 25:31.697
It's really salty!

25:43.297 --> 25:44.507
Stop!

25:49.967 --> 25:52.097
NO GOING OUT!

25:52.677 --> 25:55.477
You said you'd come right back.

25:59.267 --> 26:00.977
Do it again, and you'll lose this.

26:01.727 --> 26:02.567
Sorry.

26:10.867 --> 26:12.157
Why did you come with me?

26:16.157 --> 26:19.917
I have a weakness
for anyone longing for the sea.

26:21.457 --> 26:24.917
I love seeing schools of fish swimming,

26:25.007 --> 26:26.297
so I often go diving.

26:27.377 --> 26:29.427
I even work at a diving shop.

26:30.637 --> 26:32.427
You've swum underwater?

26:33.007 --> 26:34.217
Alongside real fish?

26:35.017 --> 26:35.847
Yeah.

26:37.137 --> 26:38.437
Wow.

26:41.517 --> 26:44.817
Tell me, are there
other places you want to go?

26:47.487 --> 26:51.067
Grandma takes a nap between one and three.

27:29.857 --> 27:31.907
First crepe ever?

27:33.487 --> 27:36.367
No, I've eaten many with my boyfriends.

27:37.657 --> 27:39.197
I'm popular with boys.

27:39.287 --> 27:41.867
I've had five boyfriends at once.

27:41.957 --> 27:42.827
Sure.

27:53.137 --> 27:54.427
Ready and…

28:02.387 --> 28:03.227
You okay?

28:06.937 --> 28:09.437
So many different blues!

28:11.777 --> 28:12.817
Let's ride that!

28:12.907 --> 28:14.447
No, wait!

28:14.527 --> 28:15.567
Hurry up!

28:16.157 --> 28:19.367
This is amazing! Where's my house?

28:19.447 --> 28:22.457
Osaka Castle? Tell me, My Servant.

28:26.207 --> 28:27.667
Afraid of heights?

28:43.387 --> 28:44.307
There.

28:45.187 --> 28:48.227
Guess what, Grandma. I made dinner.

28:48.317 --> 28:49.267
You what?

28:51.607 --> 28:53.487
Yukichi, come here.

28:54.277 --> 28:55.317
Yukichi?

28:56.317 --> 28:57.447
Yeah, I named him.

28:57.527 --> 28:58.407
Well, you can't!

28:59.277 --> 29:01.997
-Make this chair two millimeters higher.
-What?

29:09.287 --> 29:10.707
That wasn't bad.

29:10.797 --> 29:12.007
Like I told you.

29:19.967 --> 29:21.387
Stop that!

29:22.057 --> 29:23.847
Easy.

29:30.267 --> 29:32.857
Slow down!

29:37.527 --> 29:39.407
We're in the sea.

29:40.027 --> 29:41.157
A seal!

29:41.237 --> 29:42.657
California sea lion.

29:43.247 --> 29:44.327
It's got horns.

29:44.407 --> 29:45.537
It's a Naso unicornis.

29:45.617 --> 29:47.417
Look at the big one!

29:47.497 --> 29:48.577
Whale shark.

29:49.167 --> 29:50.417
What's that group?

29:50.497 --> 29:51.547
Horse mackerel.

29:52.207 --> 29:54.297
One type sticks to reefs,

29:54.377 --> 29:57.627
but another type swims in the open seas.

29:57.717 --> 30:00.467
The latter form unique schools

30:00.547 --> 30:03.177
at middle to low ocean depths.

30:03.267 --> 30:05.597
They differ in shape, color, and habitat.

30:05.677 --> 30:08.767
Gold and black mackerel stick to reefs.

30:08.847 --> 30:11.067
Rockfish take to the open sea.

30:27.917 --> 30:30.627
It's a job opportunity for Kumiko.

30:30.707 --> 30:32.457
You're as pesky as the rest.

30:34.337 --> 30:37.217
She must be able
to live an independent life.

30:37.297 --> 30:41.097
You're supposed to support, not lecture.

30:41.177 --> 30:43.887
I'm sick and tired of hearing that.

30:45.637 --> 30:48.387
Keeping her confined to the home

30:48.477 --> 30:50.977
is not in her best interests.

30:51.897 --> 30:56.027
I'd bet her departed parents
are worried too.

30:56.107 --> 30:57.567
What do you know?

30:59.947 --> 31:02.947
I refuse to take Kumiko outside.

31:05.537 --> 31:08.827
But she goes out a lot lately.

31:09.787 --> 31:12.747
She thinks I don't know.

31:12.827 --> 31:13.877
By herself?

31:16.417 --> 31:20.297
I honestly didn't think
he'd take her to places.

31:20.377 --> 31:21.887
I was flabbergasted.

31:22.467 --> 31:25.597
You'd be surprised if you saw her now.

31:26.097 --> 31:29.267
She looks like that Glico billboard.

31:29.347 --> 31:30.187
Sorry?

31:33.227 --> 31:35.977
Ready to take off at a sprint.

31:39.857 --> 31:42.697
MACARTHUR'S ASSASSIN
RED SEA

31:44.067 --> 31:45.327
It's a sea of books.

32:01.047 --> 32:01.877
"Josee"?

32:04.717 --> 32:06.007
Oh, it's you, My Servant.

32:07.007 --> 32:08.347
Does that say "Josee"?

32:09.307 --> 32:11.307
It's the main character's name.

32:12.687 --> 32:14.597
Francoise Sagan.

32:16.357 --> 32:18.937
That's the sequel to this one,

32:19.027 --> 32:22.027
the conclusion I've longed to read.

32:23.197 --> 32:25.487
Hmm, it'll put me to sleep.

32:26.777 --> 32:29.657
I wouldn't expect a boorish servant

32:29.737 --> 32:30.907
to understand Sagan.

32:31.787 --> 32:33.207
Go borrow these.

32:34.867 --> 32:36.377
We need a library card.

32:38.047 --> 32:40.207
LOST PROFILE

32:41.757 --> 32:43.337
First time?

32:44.927 --> 32:47.177
Please fill out this form.

32:51.927 --> 32:53.517
Do you like Sagan?

33:01.067 --> 33:02.397
So do I!

33:02.487 --> 33:04.317
Which is your favorite?

33:07.237 --> 33:10.827
Sorry, I never meet other Sagan fans.

33:10.907 --> 33:12.197
I got a little excited.

33:14.997 --> 33:17.577
Those Without Shadows.

33:18.457 --> 33:19.917
Cool.

33:20.497 --> 33:24.087
Have you read The Unmade Bed?
The protagonist is Beatrice

33:24.167 --> 33:26.297
-from Those Without Shadows.
-Josee, borrow them both.

33:27.837 --> 33:28.677
Boyfriend?

33:29.507 --> 33:32.267
He called you "Josee." How wonderful.

33:34.477 --> 33:37.477
No! He's not my boyfriend or anything!

33:38.477 --> 33:40.267
She wouldn't waste time on me.

33:40.817 --> 33:42.567
Boys like her.

33:42.647 --> 33:44.897
She had five boyfriends at once.

33:44.987 --> 33:47.067
Shut up. I'll beat you senseless.

33:50.577 --> 33:53.827
But I'd like to read
the book you were mentioning.

33:53.907 --> 33:55.407
Yes, about Beatrice.

33:58.827 --> 34:00.377
You made a friend.

34:00.997 --> 34:01.877
A friend?

34:02.457 --> 34:03.667
The librarian.

34:03.757 --> 34:06.587
Kana and I are already friends?

34:06.677 --> 34:08.387
It looked like it to me.

34:15.387 --> 34:18.057
Kana and I are the same age.

34:18.847 --> 34:20.517
How old is that?

34:20.607 --> 34:21.517
Twenty-four.

34:21.607 --> 34:22.817
What? You're older…

34:23.777 --> 34:28.527
I mean, wow.
So you and Kana are the same age?

34:29.657 --> 34:31.327
It must be amazing to talk

34:32.027 --> 34:34.407
to a lot of people every day.

34:35.037 --> 34:36.827
You get used to it.

34:37.407 --> 34:40.537
I meet lots of customers
at the diving shop.

34:41.127 --> 34:42.127
Really?

34:45.797 --> 34:47.877
-Hey, it's Tsuneo…
-Hey.

34:53.927 --> 34:55.927
You must be Josee.

34:58.887 --> 35:01.397
Perfect strike.

35:01.477 --> 35:05.817
Hi, I'm Tsuneo's oldest
and dearest friend,

35:05.897 --> 35:07.067
Hayato Matsuura.

35:07.987 --> 35:09.357
What social media do you use?

35:09.447 --> 35:10.607
Easy, Hayato.

35:11.197 --> 35:12.817
I don't have one.

35:16.037 --> 35:19.707
She's a fairy. Living in analog!

35:19.787 --> 35:20.617
Knock it off.

35:21.207 --> 35:22.077
What'll we do?

35:22.747 --> 35:24.417
Sorry, I'll be right back.

35:26.627 --> 35:28.837
Welcome, ladies. Come in.

35:28.917 --> 35:30.717
You don't have to worry about him.

35:30.797 --> 35:32.217
Welcome. This way.

35:32.797 --> 35:35.137
Please take a seat.

35:40.437 --> 35:42.147
Tsuneo, you're here.

35:42.727 --> 35:43.897
Just passing by.

35:45.357 --> 35:47.687
How can I help you today?

35:47.777 --> 35:50.857
We want to get our diving licenses.

35:50.947 --> 35:51.817
I see.

35:52.567 --> 35:55.117
How do you do? I'm Mai Ninomiya.

35:55.197 --> 35:57.287
Tsuneo's told me a lot about you.

35:59.997 --> 36:03.577
If there's anything you need, please ask.

36:06.877 --> 36:09.957
Oh, yesterday I saw a clown frogfish!

36:10.547 --> 36:12.507
You took the photo yourself?

36:12.587 --> 36:15.387
No, the strong swell kept interfering.

36:17.137 --> 36:17.967
I want to leave.

36:18.967 --> 36:20.017
We just got here.

36:22.227 --> 36:23.137
Josee?

36:24.477 --> 36:25.307
Sorry.

36:28.817 --> 36:31.317
Did Josee leave already?

36:31.397 --> 36:33.317
What a rare beauty.

36:33.407 --> 36:36.827
Pale skin, modest, cute, and delicate…

36:36.907 --> 36:39.157
Get back to work.

36:39.907 --> 36:40.947
What's wrong?

36:41.037 --> 36:42.657
Nothing!

36:42.747 --> 36:46.077
You wanted to see where I work.

36:49.297 --> 36:51.757
I don't like places like this.

36:52.717 --> 36:53.757
Places like this?

36:56.887 --> 36:59.217
I don't know what there is to hate.

36:59.307 --> 37:00.267
You wouldn't!

37:00.847 --> 37:02.307
That's right. I don't!

37:17.317 --> 37:18.157
No, thanks.

37:20.487 --> 37:21.867
But alone, you…

37:26.497 --> 37:28.707
Tell him not to come anymore.

37:30.547 --> 37:31.547
What happened?

37:32.127 --> 37:33.507
Just tell him.

37:35.217 --> 37:36.967
All right, I will.

37:42.847 --> 37:44.727
I'm a mess, Yukichi.

37:50.477 --> 37:52.227
I don't have to come?

37:54.567 --> 37:55.697
I understand.

38:02.867 --> 38:04.997
No, I don't understand!

38:16.297 --> 38:18.127
Like that? I'm really proud of it.

38:23.557 --> 38:24.717
This here…

38:27.267 --> 38:28.097
Sorry.

38:29.267 --> 38:30.227
What is it?

38:32.727 --> 38:36.737
I've been granted
a scholarship to study abroad!

38:36.817 --> 38:40.527
That's great! When do you go?

38:40.617 --> 38:42.027
Next March.

38:42.617 --> 38:44.697
School starts in September,

38:45.197 --> 38:48.957
but they want me to come after I graduate.

38:49.037 --> 38:53.837
I guess we'll only have
six more months working together.

38:59.007 --> 39:00.757
You've been coming alone lately.

39:01.467 --> 39:02.547
Where's Tsuneo?

39:04.887 --> 39:07.097
Who cares about that dunderhead?

39:07.727 --> 39:09.057
Dunderhead?

39:09.637 --> 39:12.557
He's useless and takes up a lot of space.

39:13.187 --> 39:15.937
He eats like he's starving
and flirts with girls.

39:16.027 --> 39:17.187
JAPANESE NOVELS

39:17.277 --> 39:18.357
What's so funny?

39:19.147 --> 39:22.067
Sorry, but you're just so obvious.

39:22.657 --> 39:24.327
What's obvious?

39:24.407 --> 39:25.537
Kana!

39:26.117 --> 39:26.997
Hi, Rio!

39:28.907 --> 39:29.747
Read this.

39:31.287 --> 39:32.327
What's wrong?

39:32.417 --> 39:36.587
I always read to kids at this time of day.

39:37.207 --> 39:40.087
But a worker just quit on us.

39:40.167 --> 39:41.717
Anyone here?

39:41.797 --> 39:42.637
Coming!

39:43.297 --> 39:44.177
I'm sorry.

39:51.057 --> 39:52.147
Will you read to us?

39:57.187 --> 40:00.027
The Little Mermaid.

40:00.107 --> 40:02.907
This lady is going to read to us!

40:06.697 --> 40:08.327
I don't think I can…

40:08.407 --> 40:09.447
Hurry and read.

40:09.537 --> 40:10.907
-Hurry.
-We're waiting.

40:10.997 --> 40:12.457
-Keep reading.
-Please.

40:12.537 --> 40:14.167
-What's wrong?
-Come on.

40:18.627 --> 40:20.337
"On the bed of a limpid,

40:20.417 --> 40:22.967
blue sea stood a pearl palace,

40:23.047 --> 40:26.257
where six princess mermaids lived."

40:27.467 --> 40:31.727
"They loved to listen
to the king tell stories

40:31.807 --> 40:36.567
about the world they'd see
above the waves as adults."

40:36.647 --> 40:39.567
"The sky, birds,
exotic things, city lights."

40:40.147 --> 40:43.567
"The princesses waited
with eager anticipation

40:43.657 --> 40:45.317
for that day to come."

40:45.907 --> 40:47.487
"'Farewell, good prince,'

40:47.577 --> 40:50.537
the mermaid said, tossing her knife."

40:50.617 --> 40:53.457
"And she dove into the sea,

40:53.537 --> 40:57.337
where her body melted away into bubbles."

41:02.667 --> 41:04.927
I can't read stories very well.

41:06.217 --> 41:07.347
Question!

41:07.967 --> 41:10.557
What did her palace look like?

41:24.397 --> 41:26.617
Look, the mermaid palace!

41:28.157 --> 41:30.697
It really looks like a mermaid home.

41:32.327 --> 41:34.907
Josee, you're an illustrator?

41:34.997 --> 41:36.327
No way!

41:36.417 --> 41:39.207
What a shame it would be

41:39.287 --> 41:42.087
for people not to see your art.

41:42.667 --> 41:46.127
I think you should
put together a collection

41:46.217 --> 41:47.887
and get them published!

41:47.967 --> 41:48.797
I can't!

41:52.717 --> 41:53.557
Sorry.

42:00.147 --> 42:00.977
Good evening.

42:03.107 --> 42:05.987
Go home! No dunderheads allowed!

42:11.027 --> 42:12.157
What are you doing?

42:22.087 --> 42:23.837
It's pretty good, right?

42:25.377 --> 42:26.927
You made it, My Servant?

42:27.797 --> 42:29.427
Yes, Your Servant made it.

42:31.387 --> 42:33.427
No wonder it's so ugly.

42:36.847 --> 42:38.017
What's it called?

42:38.847 --> 42:39.897
It's a clarion angel.

42:41.397 --> 42:44.357
A rare species found only near Mexico.

42:46.187 --> 42:50.527
When I was a kid,
my local fish store had one,

42:51.157 --> 42:52.487
and I fell in love with it.

42:53.987 --> 42:57.907
I'd go to look at it
every day after school.

42:59.617 --> 43:02.337
When I learned it swam in schools,

43:02.417 --> 43:03.707
my interest grew more.

43:05.167 --> 43:08.377
It wants to be with family too.

43:09.717 --> 43:10.547
What do you mean?

43:11.047 --> 43:12.967
My parents are divorced.

43:14.307 --> 43:18.227
Dad left home, and Mom
was always busy working.

43:19.557 --> 43:23.767
I don't think he was sad,
though, the clarion angel.

43:25.147 --> 43:27.437
He had you come every day.

43:30.357 --> 43:33.947
I've long dreamed
of seeing him swimming in a school.

43:35.487 --> 43:38.707
It's why I've studied so hard
and saved money.

43:39.407 --> 43:41.207
They're hard to find

43:41.747 --> 43:44.287
so a brief diving vacation wouldn't do.

43:46.587 --> 43:47.707
It's a nice dream.

43:50.087 --> 43:51.507
I hope it comes true.

43:57.177 --> 43:58.927
Actually, next year…

44:00.477 --> 44:01.477
This is defective.

44:01.557 --> 44:02.847
That's odd.

44:06.517 --> 44:07.567
There, all fixed.

44:23.877 --> 44:25.957
That hurts!

44:26.037 --> 44:28.587
Why the heck did you do that?

44:48.727 --> 44:49.567
Hello!

44:56.907 --> 44:58.027
Ready to go?

45:04.707 --> 45:05.537
Kumiko!

45:08.747 --> 45:11.507
Grandma, the world isn't all scary.

45:50.497 --> 45:52.047
I'm going to have nightmares.

45:52.627 --> 45:55.467
Nightmares? You came to see this.

45:56.087 --> 46:00.047
I wanted to see
the scariest thing here with you.

46:02.887 --> 46:05.477
I thought I could do it
with you by my side.

46:06.227 --> 46:07.097
With me by your side?

46:15.277 --> 46:16.237
To hold onto.

46:18.987 --> 46:22.367
I needed something
to hold onto if I got scared.

46:27.787 --> 46:28.877
That hurts.

46:33.627 --> 46:37.427
I read a story aloud
to children the other day.

46:37.507 --> 46:39.387
You, Josee? What was it?

46:40.137 --> 46:41.257
The Little Mermaid.

46:41.347 --> 46:43.307
Wow, that's amazing.

46:45.387 --> 46:46.727
I didn't read it very well.

46:47.437 --> 46:50.017
I got so nervous, I couldn't look up.

46:51.937 --> 46:52.897
It was scary.

46:55.607 --> 46:57.817
But then I drew a picture,

46:57.897 --> 46:59.487
and the children all loved it.

47:02.407 --> 47:04.327
I want to draw more.

47:04.987 --> 47:05.827
More?

47:06.327 --> 47:09.617
As a job. I want to draw professionally.

47:11.747 --> 47:13.167
I want to give it a shot.

47:14.167 --> 47:15.297
Like what you're doing.

47:19.007 --> 47:20.507
Well, I love…

47:21.637 --> 47:22.467
your drawings.

47:24.677 --> 47:26.597
Pretty cocky for a servant.

47:29.517 --> 47:32.857
Cherry blossoms fall
like rain here in spring.

47:33.477 --> 47:35.477
My dad used to bring me.

47:36.817 --> 47:38.187
It must be beautiful.

47:39.447 --> 47:43.447
If you want to see it,
you can bring me next year.

47:45.947 --> 47:46.787
What's wrong?

47:49.247 --> 47:50.077
Nothing.

48:23.317 --> 48:26.157
Did you hear about Ms. Yamamura?

48:26.237 --> 48:29.577
She's had a bad heart for some time.

48:30.447 --> 48:32.577
And she was quite old.

48:32.667 --> 48:35.667
CHIZU YAMAMURA

48:44.257 --> 48:45.797
The morticians left.

48:48.347 --> 48:50.387
If you need to talk, I'm here.

48:51.637 --> 48:53.097
About what to do next.

48:56.557 --> 49:00.567
Grandma left me a little money to live on.

49:01.567 --> 49:03.147
I'll be okay for a while.

49:04.607 --> 49:05.447
I see.

49:07.277 --> 49:09.537
But I can't afford to pay.

49:11.537 --> 49:14.867
I can't pay My Servant wages.

49:19.877 --> 49:20.707
I understand.

50:08.887 --> 50:11.257
OUT OF OXYGEN

50:37.827 --> 50:40.747
It's rare for you
to lose track of oxygen, Tsuneo.

50:41.837 --> 50:43.877
You seem distracted.

50:43.957 --> 50:46.297
I know. You confessed--

50:48.677 --> 50:50.717
Josee's grandmother died.

50:52.507 --> 50:55.467
So now she's all alone.

50:56.307 --> 50:58.017
That's pretty harsh.

50:58.727 --> 51:00.517
And worrying.

51:02.937 --> 51:05.147
She's not a child,

51:05.647 --> 51:08.197
and there are welfare services
and facilities.

51:13.407 --> 51:15.117
"Free yourself from life."

51:16.077 --> 51:18.787
"From that which others call life."

51:19.327 --> 51:20.367
"Be free from emotion,

51:21.077 --> 51:24.627
from one's strengths,
one's own weaknesses."

51:25.207 --> 51:27.377
"Be but one momentary breath,

51:27.467 --> 51:31.297
one-millionth of a billion nebulas."

51:37.597 --> 51:40.637
Are you home, Ms. Kumiko? It's Mizushima.

51:44.937 --> 51:47.647
This is Mr. Fujita, a social worker.

51:48.397 --> 51:54.367
The resident's association chairman
got a call from one of your neighbors.

51:54.947 --> 51:57.617
They heard your grandmother passed

51:57.697 --> 51:59.707
and felt you needed assistance.

52:01.077 --> 52:02.287
It's none of their business.

52:04.627 --> 52:07.917
How do you plan to move forward?

52:09.627 --> 52:10.467
Pictures.

52:12.547 --> 52:14.717
I plan to draw pictures.

52:17.557 --> 52:22.347
You're saying you'll earn
a living as an artist?

52:23.307 --> 52:26.607
I think it's wonderful to have a dream.

52:27.187 --> 52:30.937
Dreams are one thing. Reality is another.

52:31.027 --> 52:33.567
You of all should know that.

52:34.157 --> 52:37.287
Don't be foolish. Go look for work…

52:38.657 --> 52:41.707
Your grandma's not here to dote on you.

52:42.827 --> 52:44.377
Mr. Fujita.

52:44.457 --> 52:49.797
Or is there someone else
who will support you?

53:11.187 --> 53:12.447
Are you okay?

53:15.317 --> 53:17.487
I'm Mai. We met the other day.

53:19.447 --> 53:20.287
Why are you here?

53:21.327 --> 53:25.957
I remembered Tsuneo saying
you lived by the river.

53:27.457 --> 53:31.877
It would've been faster
if we had just asked Tsuneo.

53:35.797 --> 53:36.757
What do you want?

53:42.847 --> 53:44.637
I beg you to free Tsuneo.

53:45.597 --> 53:47.937
Wait, we came to cheer her up!

53:48.017 --> 53:51.147
He's worked so hard for his dream.

53:51.727 --> 53:55.647
Studying Spanish, working to save money

53:56.147 --> 53:57.777
so he can study abroad.

53:58.367 --> 53:59.197
Study abroad?

53:59.827 --> 54:03.367
Next March, he's going to Mexico.

54:05.327 --> 54:06.327
He didn't tell you?

54:08.417 --> 54:10.707
Would you support his dream?

54:11.337 --> 54:12.377
At this rate--

54:12.457 --> 54:14.877
Why do you have to ask my permission?

54:17.047 --> 54:18.967
What's your relationship with him?

54:31.147 --> 54:32.067
It's sympathy.

54:33.777 --> 54:37.277
Tsuneo only visits you
out of pity for your condition.

54:38.317 --> 54:39.527
What the hell are you saying?

54:40.657 --> 54:41.577
Don't listen to her.

54:43.287 --> 54:44.947
Hey, wait up!

54:47.287 --> 54:49.287
What types of cytoplasm do I mean?

54:49.377 --> 54:51.837
That's right, cytoplasmic genomes.

54:52.627 --> 54:56.507
You can consider them
a place to store genomes.

55:03.007 --> 55:05.347
THE LITTLE MERMAID

55:11.897 --> 55:12.767
Hello.

55:20.407 --> 55:23.577
Josee, I brought fish-shaped cakes.

55:26.327 --> 55:27.367
Why did you come?

55:30.747 --> 55:31.577
Josee?

55:33.497 --> 55:34.337
Your room…

55:34.877 --> 55:40.627
I asked a helper to come
and clean the place once a month.

55:41.387 --> 55:42.467
And your pictures?

55:42.547 --> 55:43.387
Thrown out.

55:43.467 --> 55:44.677
What? Why?

55:45.387 --> 55:47.267
None of your business.

55:48.227 --> 55:50.267
If that's all, you can go.

56:05.527 --> 56:06.657
I'll fix it right away.

56:16.207 --> 56:17.337
I want to go to the sea.

56:20.217 --> 56:22.837
This will be your last job as My Servant.

57:01.967 --> 57:03.257
Up to the waterline?

57:03.757 --> 57:04.677
This is fine.

57:06.797 --> 57:08.057
How about a warm drink?

57:08.557 --> 57:09.387
No thanks.

57:21.527 --> 57:22.357
It's salty.

57:27.317 --> 57:28.157
Josee.

57:34.367 --> 57:37.787
I don't want money.
Don't call this the last job.

57:38.587 --> 57:39.417
Josee!

57:41.417 --> 57:42.377
I'm no longer Josee.

57:44.467 --> 57:47.297
I've taken a job in an office.

57:48.217 --> 57:50.927
You didn't need to get rid of your art.

57:51.517 --> 57:52.727
It was out of reach.

57:54.307 --> 57:55.687
Everything's always out of reach.

57:57.057 --> 57:59.147
The red balloon caught on the roof.

58:00.017 --> 58:01.897
The cicada husk on the tree.

58:03.277 --> 58:05.737
Walking under an umbrella in the rain.

58:06.237 --> 58:08.947
Climbing the steps of a shrine.

58:10.277 --> 58:11.117
All of it.

58:13.577 --> 58:16.457
I no longer wish to reach for any of it.

58:18.327 --> 58:22.457
If you really don't,
then why do you look so sad?

58:24.627 --> 58:26.167
Don't give up what you love!

58:29.637 --> 58:31.137
You're leaving soon, right?

58:38.267 --> 58:39.727
The healthy wouldn't understand.

59:15.057 --> 59:16.177
Josee!

59:20.687 --> 59:22.057
Josee!

59:41.707 --> 59:42.537
My Servant…

59:44.167 --> 59:45.127
My Servant.

59:47.797 --> 59:48.917
My Servant!

59:49.967 --> 59:51.177
My Servant!

59:53.927 --> 59:57.467
Tsuneo!

01:00:04.227 --> 01:00:05.517
Are you all right?

01:00:06.727 --> 01:00:11.027
There's been a traffic accident!

01:00:20.787 --> 01:00:22.247
-Remove the scoop.
-Yes.

01:00:22.327 --> 01:00:23.287
Cutting away clothes.

01:00:23.377 --> 01:00:27.377
Pulse 120, BP 70 over 40, saturation 94%.

01:00:27.457 --> 01:00:29.457
Maintain ten liters of oxygen.

01:00:29.547 --> 01:00:30.877
-Peripheral off?
-Not yet.

01:00:30.967 --> 01:00:33.007
Quickly, 18-gauge, full throttle.

01:00:33.087 --> 01:00:37.007
-Crossmatch. Don't forget the blood gas.
-Got it.

01:00:37.097 --> 01:00:38.637
X-ray standby!

01:00:39.267 --> 01:00:41.227
Airways clear, respiration's steady.

01:00:41.307 --> 01:00:42.977
Starting echo.

01:00:43.057 --> 01:00:44.597
Negative. Pneumothorax is fine.

01:00:45.857 --> 01:00:46.687
Mr. Suzukawa?

01:00:46.767 --> 01:00:50.527
Mr. Tsuneo Suzukawa? Can you hear me?

01:00:50.607 --> 01:00:53.857
If you can hear me, open your eyes.

01:01:16.797 --> 01:01:17.717
Are you awake?

01:01:18.807 --> 01:01:19.967
Yes.

01:01:20.057 --> 01:01:22.847
You were in a traffic accident.
This is a hospital.

01:01:24.347 --> 01:01:25.557
I'll call the doctor.

01:01:28.477 --> 01:01:31.027
The girl in the wheelchair?

01:01:31.107 --> 01:01:34.647
Oh, yes, we asked her to go home today.

01:01:34.737 --> 01:01:37.827
She insisted on waiting till you awoke.

01:01:38.527 --> 01:01:40.487
So she's not injured?

01:01:40.577 --> 01:01:41.407
No.

01:01:44.457 --> 01:01:45.827
How do you feel?

01:01:46.617 --> 01:01:48.457
I was in an accident?

01:01:49.247 --> 01:01:51.297
You suffered a concussion,

01:01:51.377 --> 01:01:53.837
but tests showed nothing was wrong.

01:01:54.467 --> 01:01:57.297
Your internal organs are sound,

01:01:58.297 --> 01:02:01.807
but your right shinbone
is broken at the ankle.

01:02:03.057 --> 01:02:04.557
In short, an open fracture.

01:02:05.347 --> 01:02:07.477
Emergency surgery was done

01:02:07.557 --> 01:02:10.017
to prevent infection at the wound.

01:02:10.567 --> 01:02:14.187
We secured the fracture
with screws and a plate.

01:02:14.817 --> 01:02:19.697
It'll take two months
before it can bear your weight.

01:02:20.367 --> 01:02:21.487
Two months.

01:02:22.287 --> 01:02:23.577
One more thing.

01:02:23.657 --> 01:02:29.327
Surgery couldn't unite
the joint surfaces perfectly.

01:02:29.417 --> 01:02:31.837
There's a risk of osteoarthritis.

01:02:32.747 --> 01:02:34.707
Osteoarthritis?

01:02:35.797 --> 01:02:40.347
You could experience
joint pain and stiffness,

01:02:40.427 --> 01:02:43.427
making it hard to walk or run like before.

01:02:44.637 --> 01:02:47.347
The hairline fracture in your left arm

01:02:47.437 --> 01:02:51.687
may make crutches moot for a while.

01:02:54.187 --> 01:02:55.237
Will I heal?

01:02:57.777 --> 01:03:00.157
It's hard to say at this stage.

01:03:15.127 --> 01:03:15.957
Josee.

01:03:17.127 --> 01:03:18.177
I'm sorry.

01:03:21.847 --> 01:03:22.927
It's not your fault.

01:03:25.677 --> 01:03:28.187
I seem to be in pretty bad shape.

01:03:29.227 --> 01:03:31.937
Even rehab might not fix everything.

01:03:34.897 --> 01:03:38.397
If it turns out I can't walk again, I…

01:03:46.487 --> 01:03:47.447
I need to sleep.

01:04:04.507 --> 01:04:05.347
Quiet!

01:04:20.147 --> 01:04:22.237
You don't need to come, Mom.

01:04:22.737 --> 01:04:24.317
You'll hurt your back.

01:04:24.987 --> 01:04:26.867
It's no big deal, I swear.

01:04:28.117 --> 01:04:32.617
I'll come visit
after I leave the hospital. See you.

01:04:35.877 --> 01:04:36.707
Professor.

01:04:39.007 --> 01:04:40.797
How are you, Tsuneo?

01:04:41.377 --> 01:04:43.837
I'm sorry to worry you.

01:04:46.887 --> 01:04:49.307
Listen, about your study abroad.

01:04:50.727 --> 01:04:53.187
They'd like another student

01:04:53.267 --> 01:04:55.767
to come in March if you can't.

01:04:57.567 --> 01:05:01.317
It's a pity,
but you'll get another chance.

01:05:02.027 --> 01:05:05.317
For now, just focus on getting well.

01:05:10.077 --> 01:05:11.077
That's not the problem.

01:05:12.907 --> 01:05:16.327
It's possible I may not
be able to dive anymore.

01:05:18.747 --> 01:05:23.547
If I can't do that,
I'll lose my reason for going abroad.

01:05:33.887 --> 01:05:37.437
SPANISH GRAMMAR

01:06:05.257 --> 01:06:07.217
So rotate your ankle

01:06:07.297 --> 01:06:11.557
and extend your toes
to the extent possible.

01:06:12.177 --> 01:06:15.017
When the swelling goes down,

01:06:15.097 --> 01:06:18.767
we can shift to your rehabilitation.

01:06:21.437 --> 01:06:22.277
Tsuneo.

01:06:24.187 --> 01:06:25.317
I bought pudding.

01:06:27.317 --> 01:06:28.197
Thanks.

01:06:30.487 --> 01:06:32.197
Starting rehab already?

01:06:33.407 --> 01:06:34.247
Yeah.

01:06:35.037 --> 01:06:36.827
I'll put this in the fridge.

01:06:38.627 --> 01:06:43.507
My parents keep sending
rice and vegetables.

01:06:43.587 --> 01:06:45.917
My fridge is bulging.

01:06:46.007 --> 01:06:47.757
SPANISH GRAMMAR

01:06:54.097 --> 01:06:56.387
Want to get some fresh air?

01:07:09.027 --> 01:07:11.157
Feel free to say what's on your mind.

01:07:12.487 --> 01:07:14.157
I'm here to give you my support.

01:07:16.947 --> 01:07:21.417
It doesn't matter anymore…
Studying abroad, Mexico.

01:07:23.587 --> 01:07:27.087
I thought I was stronger than this.

01:07:28.467 --> 01:07:30.087
Please don't give up.

01:07:30.177 --> 01:07:31.587
Work hard on rehab--

01:07:31.677 --> 01:07:34.387
"Work hard"? What if it doesn't matter?

01:07:36.887 --> 01:07:39.517
I didn't understand anything.

01:07:40.937 --> 01:07:44.647
How scary it is
to reach for something I want.

01:07:51.357 --> 01:07:53.657
I…

01:07:53.737 --> 01:07:54.657
have feelings for you, Tsuneo!

01:07:55.947 --> 01:07:58.327
I just didn't want that

01:07:58.407 --> 01:08:01.457
to get in the way of your goals.

01:08:03.707 --> 01:08:04.917
But I can't help it.

01:08:06.917 --> 01:08:08.967
I'm madly in love with you!

01:08:15.967 --> 01:08:17.347
How'd this happen?

01:08:19.347 --> 01:08:21.227
Mai, listen. I--

01:08:21.307 --> 01:08:22.437
I know.

01:08:23.857 --> 01:08:26.567
I don't need a "Sorry" or a "Thanks."

01:08:27.357 --> 01:08:30.527
I hate women who cry in front of men.

01:08:34.367 --> 01:08:35.277
But…

01:08:37.787 --> 01:08:39.077
I needed to say it.

01:08:48.297 --> 01:08:49.877
We should get back.

01:09:10.567 --> 01:09:12.947
I know you're there! Answer the door!

01:09:18.027 --> 01:09:19.037
If you don't…

01:09:21.117 --> 01:09:21.947
Go away!

01:09:24.077 --> 01:09:25.037
Don't come back.

01:09:28.037 --> 01:09:30.507
Tsuneo's given up on studying abroad.

01:09:32.507 --> 01:09:34.337
So now I'm making him mine.

01:09:35.257 --> 01:09:39.467
I'll give him the love
he needs to forget the sea.

01:09:41.637 --> 01:09:44.347
I never wanted him to go to Mexico.

01:09:45.977 --> 01:09:48.227
I prayed he'd forget his silly dream

01:09:49.357 --> 01:09:53.447
and stay near me.
I wanted to be by his side.

01:09:55.907 --> 01:09:57.867
I know him so much better than you.

01:09:58.907 --> 01:10:03.287
His love for talking about fish,
the awful way he hums.

01:10:04.207 --> 01:10:06.037
He's bad at rock-paper-scissors.

01:10:07.417 --> 01:10:10.667
He likes pudding, hates cucumbers,

01:10:10.747 --> 01:10:13.507
and always has ice-cold hands.

01:10:15.837 --> 01:10:18.637
I could name a hundred more things.

01:10:18.717 --> 01:10:21.427
I know him far better.

01:10:23.927 --> 01:10:25.637
Well, say something!

01:10:27.517 --> 01:10:29.557
My Servant's never giving up.

01:10:30.147 --> 01:10:34.437
He'll never forget
about fish or abandon his dream!

01:10:35.027 --> 01:10:36.197
That's who he is!

01:10:37.147 --> 01:10:38.777
You know that, right?

01:10:41.027 --> 01:10:44.407
I can't name a hundred things about him.

01:10:46.497 --> 01:10:49.037
But you can't beat my feelings for him.

01:10:51.337 --> 01:10:53.627
If that's true, then show it!

01:11:09.017 --> 01:11:10.097
Salty.

01:11:19.607 --> 01:11:21.027
You're clumsy.

01:11:22.617 --> 01:11:24.197
I'm a good woman.

01:11:29.417 --> 01:11:33.087
Why don't you buy me dinner then?

01:11:33.167 --> 01:11:33.997
What?

01:12:09.997 --> 01:12:10.827
Josee.

01:12:13.787 --> 01:12:14.917
I have a request.

01:12:26.717 --> 01:12:30.767
You should let the characters
show more emotions.

01:12:31.437 --> 01:12:32.897
Say how they feel.

01:12:33.807 --> 01:12:34.647
I see.

01:13:12.057 --> 01:13:13.097
Hey, redhead.

01:13:14.227 --> 01:13:15.147
Josee?

01:13:16.857 --> 01:13:17.767
Lend me your face.

01:13:18.977 --> 01:13:20.027
What?

01:13:20.107 --> 01:13:23.317
LOST PROFILE

01:13:24.447 --> 01:13:28.827
I desired nothing but my escape from him.

01:13:29.617 --> 01:13:30.747
That is all.

01:13:32.247 --> 01:13:36.037
Upon reflection,
it was truly a pitiful story.

01:13:44.757 --> 01:13:45.637
It's done.

01:13:46.217 --> 01:13:47.047
Ta-da.

01:13:50.807 --> 01:13:52.017
What's this?

01:13:52.097 --> 01:13:54.687
Isn't it obvious? Permission to leave.

01:13:55.687 --> 01:13:57.727
No, why do you have it?

01:13:57.807 --> 01:14:00.147
I just figured you might seek

01:14:00.227 --> 01:14:02.857
a change of pace once in a while.

01:14:05.237 --> 01:14:08.117
I'm sorry, but I'm not in the mood.

01:14:08.197 --> 01:14:12.447
Don't be such a bore, Tsuneo.
Let's have some fun!

01:14:12.537 --> 01:14:13.707
Leave me alone!

01:14:19.837 --> 01:14:23.757
As your diving buddy,
it's my job to give you oxygen…

01:14:25.837 --> 01:14:29.677
whenever you need it.
So shut up and follow me.

01:14:36.887 --> 01:14:38.147
What's going on?

01:14:38.227 --> 01:14:39.307
Don't ask questions.

01:14:44.277 --> 01:14:45.107
This place.

01:15:03.667 --> 01:15:08.047
THE MERMAID AND THE SHINY WING

01:15:09.007 --> 01:15:13.177
The Mermaid and the Shiny Wing.

01:15:22.897 --> 01:15:25.227
From the floor of the deep blue sea,

01:15:25.317 --> 01:15:27.527
festive music is heard.

01:15:28.197 --> 01:15:30.777
It's a mermaid's 20th birthday

01:15:30.867 --> 01:15:34.117
when she can leave the sea.

01:15:38.997 --> 01:15:39.867
You're doing fine.

01:15:47.087 --> 01:15:51.887
The mermaid received
a magic shell as a gift.

01:15:53.007 --> 01:15:54.387
And it spoke to her.

01:15:54.967 --> 01:15:57.977
"You can use me to turn human,

01:15:58.057 --> 01:15:59.887
and back into a mermaid again."

01:16:01.057 --> 01:16:04.727
"But you must not wish for anything else."

01:16:05.397 --> 01:16:07.227
"For if you do,

01:16:08.737 --> 01:16:11.317
you'll turn to froth and vanish forever."

01:16:12.907 --> 01:16:16.737
"I understand,"
said the mermaid and swam ashore.

01:16:18.117 --> 01:16:21.287
"Oh, shell, turn me into a human."

01:16:23.247 --> 01:16:26.497
Suddenly, her fins became graceful legs.

01:16:27.497 --> 01:16:31.507
"How wonderful,"
she exclaimed as she climbed a hill.

01:16:32.587 --> 01:16:35.677
But the world outside was full of danger.

01:16:37.257 --> 01:16:40.517
A ferocious tiger appeared before her.

01:16:42.137 --> 01:16:44.187
The mermaid tried to run

01:16:45.107 --> 01:16:47.357
but lost her footing and fell.

01:16:48.437 --> 01:16:52.697
Clinging to a rock, she yelled, "Help!"

01:16:54.407 --> 01:16:58.237
Just then, a young man
with pure white wings

01:16:58.327 --> 01:17:01.037
descended from the sky to help.

01:17:02.037 --> 01:17:04.247
"Thank you. Those are lovely wings."

01:17:05.167 --> 01:17:08.377
The young man
beamed happily at those words.

01:17:09.587 --> 01:17:12.927
"When spring comes,
I'm taking flight with them."

01:17:13.967 --> 01:17:16.047
For he had a dream.

01:17:18.007 --> 01:17:22.557
It was to fly
to a shiny sea far, far away.

01:17:23.477 --> 01:17:27.187
A place where a family
of bright orange fish swam.

01:17:27.937 --> 01:17:30.067
A vast sea, full of fun and frolic.

01:17:31.567 --> 01:17:35.607
The two became friends
and went to many places together.

01:17:36.987 --> 01:17:40.537
"Every place makes my heart
dance with such joy,

01:17:40.617 --> 01:17:42.197
I feel like skipping."

01:17:43.207 --> 01:17:46.497
The mermaid saw her world grow and expand.

01:17:47.957 --> 01:17:50.547
The seasons changed and spring arrived.

01:17:51.417 --> 01:17:55.257
The day for
the young man's departure came.

01:17:55.967 --> 01:18:00.767
The mermaid was sad
and walked alone in the woods.

01:18:01.637 --> 01:18:05.897
Again, a ferocious tiger
appeared before her.

01:18:06.847 --> 01:18:10.477
Claws sharp, fangs bared,
it pounced on the mermaid.

01:18:11.067 --> 01:18:13.397
"Look out," cried the young man,

01:18:13.487 --> 01:18:16.197
appearing just in time to save her.

01:18:17.067 --> 01:18:19.907
But this time, he was injured,

01:18:20.527 --> 01:18:23.077
his gorgeous wings, broken.

01:18:24.617 --> 01:18:26.667
Sobbing with grief,

01:18:27.167 --> 01:18:30.667
the mermaid took
the magic shell in her hands

01:18:31.997 --> 01:18:34.757
and wished, "Please save him."

01:18:36.547 --> 01:18:39.467
Within seconds, his wounds healed

01:18:40.007 --> 01:18:41.757
and the youth awoke alive and well,

01:18:42.637 --> 01:18:45.887
but his wings would never return.

01:18:47.057 --> 01:18:52.687
"I can no longer reach
the shiny sea," he lamented.

01:18:53.397 --> 01:18:55.067
The mermaid said, "Raise your head."

01:18:56.107 --> 01:18:59.567
"You have larger wings in your heart."

01:19:00.987 --> 01:19:03.487
"With those wings, you sheltered me

01:19:04.327 --> 01:19:06.957
and used them to push me forward."

01:19:07.827 --> 01:19:11.957
"With wings of the heart,
you can fly anywhere."

01:19:13.497 --> 01:19:17.127
The young man set off
for the shiny sea by boat.

01:19:18.297 --> 01:19:20.887
In driving rain or stormy winds,

01:19:20.967 --> 01:19:23.057
he pushed ever forward.

01:19:23.847 --> 01:19:27.807
"I'm not afraid
for I'm in pursuit of my dreams."

01:19:28.807 --> 01:19:34.567
His heart wings were
strong, supple, and beautiful.

01:19:34.647 --> 01:19:36.437
And most of all, unbreakable.

01:19:37.607 --> 01:19:40.027
At last, he found the shiny sea.

01:19:41.317 --> 01:19:43.987
With great joy, he dove into it.

01:19:44.077 --> 01:19:48.367
He started swimming freely
with the orange fish,

01:19:49.617 --> 01:19:52.747
so happy that his dream came true.

01:19:54.207 --> 01:19:58.217
"Oh, shell, you can now
turn me into bubbles."

01:20:00.007 --> 01:20:03.717
But her legs turned back into fins

01:20:03.797 --> 01:20:06.347
and nothing else occurred.

01:20:07.717 --> 01:20:09.307
The magic shell spoke.

01:20:10.347 --> 01:20:11.647
"Wishing for another's benefit

01:20:12.187 --> 01:20:16.397
and not your own
will never make you vanish."

01:20:19.527 --> 01:20:24.117
So with a heart filled
with shiny jewels of memories,

01:20:24.197 --> 01:20:27.487
the mermaid returned to the deep blue sea.

01:20:29.037 --> 01:20:29.867
The end.

01:22:17.847 --> 01:22:19.147
Why are you hiding?

01:22:27.027 --> 01:22:28.487
Look, I think he can make it!

01:22:44.877 --> 01:22:46.927
-You did it!
-You did it!

01:22:58.687 --> 01:23:01.317
Yukichi, My Servant walked today.

01:23:04.937 --> 01:23:06.987
Stray cats must not get spoiled.

01:23:15.077 --> 01:23:16.327
Must not get spoiled.

01:23:18.997 --> 01:23:20.827
Fight the tiger yourself.

01:23:24.877 --> 01:23:25.957
I'm getting out!

01:23:27.667 --> 01:23:30.717
I just need to make weekly visits.

01:23:31.507 --> 01:23:35.217
That's great. Congrats!

01:23:36.637 --> 01:23:37.477
Thanks.

01:23:40.187 --> 01:23:42.517
I'm not sure about the side effects yet,

01:23:43.727 --> 01:23:46.567
but I'm going to Mexico no matter what.

01:23:48.567 --> 01:23:50.657
Now that I've got heart wings.

01:23:55.197 --> 01:23:56.657
You'll be fine.

01:24:00.327 --> 01:24:03.337
They're letting me leave on the 24th.

01:24:04.497 --> 01:24:06.877
Can you come get me?

01:24:07.457 --> 01:24:08.417
10 a.m.

01:24:13.297 --> 01:24:14.137
Josee?

01:24:17.097 --> 01:24:19.187
I'm just so happy.

01:24:21.147 --> 01:24:21.977
Thank you.

01:25:47.227 --> 01:25:48.057
Josee?

01:26:03.077 --> 01:26:04.037
Josee!

01:26:27.397 --> 01:26:28.227
Josee.

01:26:29.937 --> 01:26:30.767
Here.

01:26:35.947 --> 01:26:36.777
Ms. Kana!

01:26:37.277 --> 01:26:39.947
Tsuneo, congrats on getting out.

01:26:40.777 --> 01:26:41.737
Where's Josee?

01:26:41.827 --> 01:26:43.447
I haven't seen her today.

01:26:45.707 --> 01:26:46.537
Sorry.

01:26:47.787 --> 01:26:49.247
You're so right.

01:26:51.297 --> 01:26:53.207
Big trouble! Josee's missing!

01:27:21.027 --> 01:27:23.947
A girl in a wheelchair just boarded.

01:27:25.537 --> 01:27:27.497
Do you know where to?

01:28:24.507 --> 01:28:26.467
Attention, guests.

01:28:27.847 --> 01:28:30.557
The zoo will be closing in a few minutes.

01:28:31.477 --> 01:28:37.397
Please make sure you have
all your belongings with you.

01:29:36.497 --> 01:29:37.377
Josee.

01:29:54.057 --> 01:29:54.897
Stop!

01:29:57.187 --> 01:29:58.017
Sorry!

01:30:15.867 --> 01:30:16.957
Josee!

01:30:30.887 --> 01:30:31.967
That hurts.

01:30:34.767 --> 01:30:37.057
You all right, Josee?

01:30:38.267 --> 01:30:39.857
Are you okay yourself?

01:30:43.987 --> 01:30:44.817
Your leg.

01:30:45.737 --> 01:30:47.357
You just got out.

01:30:49.027 --> 01:30:52.907
In my panic to find you,
I found myself running.

01:30:54.247 --> 01:30:55.077
Why?

01:31:00.457 --> 01:31:02.837
I've decided to try to become

01:31:02.917 --> 01:31:04.837
a picture book illustrator.

01:31:06.047 --> 01:31:07.877
I plan to stand on my own two feet.

01:31:10.177 --> 01:31:14.637
You've pushed me
from behind for long enough.

01:31:14.727 --> 01:31:15.767
It's not for you.

01:31:18.307 --> 01:31:19.647
It wasn't for you.

01:31:21.397 --> 01:31:23.227
I want to be Your Servant.

01:31:26.317 --> 01:31:28.527
What about the clarion angel?

01:31:29.107 --> 01:31:31.067
And going to Mexico?

01:31:31.617 --> 01:31:33.617
I'll still go, but…

01:31:35.117 --> 01:31:36.157
I love you, Josee!

01:31:45.297 --> 01:31:46.127
I…

01:31:48.217 --> 01:31:49.047
I…

01:31:52.677 --> 01:31:54.217
love you too, My Servant.

01:32:22.327 --> 01:32:24.377
It's not at all like I imagined.

01:32:25.997 --> 01:32:28.377
What? In a bad way?

01:32:30.927 --> 01:32:32.217
In a good way.

01:37:23.127 --> 01:37:24.717
-Pretty, right?
-Yes.

01:37:29.517 --> 01:37:31.227
It's really a cherry blossom rain.

01:37:37.687 --> 01:37:39.067
Did you die?

01:37:39.727 --> 01:37:40.607
What?

01:37:40.687 --> 01:37:41.987
Are you a ghost?

01:37:42.697 --> 01:37:44.487
I'm home for spring break.

01:37:44.567 --> 01:37:45.657
You didn't tell me!

01:37:46.567 --> 01:37:48.737
I wanted to surprise you.

01:37:52.327 --> 01:37:54.037
Pretty cocky for a servant.
